config KSHRINK_LRUVECD
       bool "Support async lruvecd shrink"
       default y
       help
         Asynchronous shrink lruvecd optimization feature.
         Pages whose trylock was contended during vmscan are marked
         and reclaimed later by a dedicated kthread, instead of
         stalling the reclaim path.
         
         This version implements pressure-adaptive behavior:
         - Dynamic queue limits (8/16/32 MiB based on memory pressure)
         - Bounded batch processing to reduce lock contention
         - Pressure-adaptive scheduling and CPU affinity
         - Comprehensive runtime statistics via /proc/kshrink_lruvecd_status
